<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best World Drop Items for Restoration Druid</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="the-celestial-court">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_pet_tigergodcub.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> The Celestial Court</span></h3>Chi-ji, Yu'Lon, Xuen, and Niuzao all share a loot pool and drop item level 553 Tier 16. They are worth clearing to see if you get lucky! We won't be planning around getting gear from them, though, because it is quite unlikely we can build anything approaching a full tier set.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="ordos">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_axe_1h_firelandsraid_d_02.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Ordos, Fire God of the Yaungol</span></h3>Ordos drops some decent pieces, such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90435/ring-of-wretched-flames">
<img alt="Ring of Wretched Flames" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_145.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Wretched Flames</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=90430/stomphowl-pendant">
<img alt="Stomphowl Pendant" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_108.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stomphowl Pendant</span></a>. These are fairly rare, but can be nice items until you obtain your Celestial gear.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops-2">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_staff_2h_pandarenmonk_c_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Timeless Isle Items for Restoration Druid</span></h2>The Timeless Isle in Phase 5 is great for catching up on gear.  You will earn <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=777/timeless-coin">
<span>
<img alt="Timeless Coin" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/timelesscoin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Timeless Coin</span></span></a> for almost all activities that you participate in.  You can pick up <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103988/contemplation-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Contemplation of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_cranegod.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Contemplation of Chi-Ji</span></a> to sort a trinket slot, and other pieces like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105923/contemplation-of-shaohao">
<img alt="Contemplation of Shaohao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_2h_pandung_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Contemplation of Shaohao</span></a> can help boost your item level while you farm Celestial dungeons for your other slots, but its level is not high enough to wear for long.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Restoration Druid Trinkets</span></h2>Our pre-raid trinkets are fairly restrained, and you'll want to grab Celestial trinkets when possible.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103988/contemplation-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Contemplation of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_cranegod.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Contemplation of Chi-Ji</span></a> <i>(Timeless Coins)</i> - A good starter trinket you can obtain very easily without stepping foot in a raid or dungeon.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102299/prismatic-prison-of-pride">
<img alt="Prismatic Prison of Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Prismatic Prison of Pride</span></a> <i>(Sha of Pride)</i> - A very powerful trinket that replaces typical passive intellect with an interesting secondary stat amplification. It lets us hit breakpoints more easily, and greatly increases the amount of Spirit and Mastery we'll have. It is a bit weaker when you're still gearing and you might find a flat intellect alternative below gives you more immediate power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102309/dysmorphic-samophlange-of-discontinuity">
<img alt="Dysmorphic Samophlange of Discontinuity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dysmorphic Samophlange of Discontinuity</span></a> <i>(Siegecrafted Blackfuse)</i> - The raids premier regeneration trinket. This is the most straightforward choice for your second trinket slot, and has the least variance, though it also has much smaller peaks than the alternatives below.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102304/thoks-acid-grooved-tooth">
<img alt="Thok's Acid-Grooved Tooth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Acid-Grooved Tooth</span></a> <i>(Thok the Bloodthirsty)</i> - While the cleave effect is absurdly strong on paper, it has a very small range. You will likely find this trinket is situationally your best-in-slot, but dependent on how stacked your raid is. The cleave will duplicate the entire heal, and works on all of our healing except some Force of Nature abilities.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102294/nazgrims-burnished-insignia">
<img alt="Nazgrim's Burnished Insignia" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nazgrim's Burnished Insignia</span></a> <i>(General Nazgrim)</i> - Much lower variance than the cleave trinket above though also less powerful if the raid is stacked. Consider it a reasonable alternative for spread raid groups.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102293/purified-bindings-of-immerseus">
<img alt="Purified Bindings of Immerseus" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Bindings of Immerseus</span></a> <i>(Immerseus)</i> - Another amplification effect is good in theory, but we have no clear way to proc the second effect without awkward Cat Form plays.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Restoration Druid</span></h2>In Phase 5, you can at last finish the Legendary Quest Line and earn your Legendary Cloak. We only have one choice in <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102247/jina-kang-kindness-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Jina-Kang, Kindness of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_cranehealer_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jina-Kang, Kindness of Chi-Ji</span></a>. Over the course of a fight, it puts in a decent amount of work and the effect is very good while active. The only downside is that the proc rate is low and so variance can feel high. You can read more about how to finish the questline and obtain the cloak <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/raids/legendary-cloak-questline-overview">here</a>. With the removal of Raid Finder in Mists of Pandaria Classic, it is possible to earn your Legendary Cloak without ever setting foot into a raid.  This can be done inside Celestial Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Restoration Druids in Phase 3</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="emperor-shaohao">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_pandarenserpentgodmount_gold.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Emperor Shaohao</span></h3>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>Emperor Shaohao is a new faction introduced on the Timeless Isle.  This faction is purely for vanity loot only.<br/>
<br/>Reputation gear is of quite high item level (even higher than Celestial Dungeons) but costs <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, which is limited. In Phase 3 you can mostly ignore reputations outside of Shado-Pan Assault since they take quite a while to grind to a good reputation level and catch up gear is better anyway.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="shado-pan-assault">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Shado-Pan Assault</span></h3>Shado-Pan Assault is a new faction in 5.5.2 that offers some very nice item level rewards - even at the Friendly reputation level.<br/>
<br/>
