<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Restoration Druids</span></h2>Most crafted items are no longer restricted by profession which means we're able to wear leatherworking crafted items even if we aren't leatherworkers.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-3-crafts-high-level-might-be-expensive">Phase 3 Crafts (High level, might be expensive)</h4>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94273/spirit-keeper-footguards">
<img alt="Spirit Keeper Footguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirit Keeper Footguards</span></a> (Leatherworking - requires a Raid material).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94274/spirit-keeper-helm">
<img alt="Spirit Keeper Helm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirit Keeper Helm</span></a> (Leatherworking - requires a Raid material).</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-1-2-crafts-lower-level-much-cheaper">Phase 1/<wbr/>2 Crafts (Lower level, much cheaper)</h4>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85849/wildblood-gloves">
<img alt="Wildblood Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wildblood Gloves</span></a> (Leatherworking).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85850/wildblood-vest">
<img alt="Wildblood Vest" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wildblood Vest</span></a> (Leatherworking).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85827/liferuned-leather-gloves">
<img alt="Liferuned Leather Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Liferuned Leather Gloves</span></a> (Leatherworking - requires a phase 1 Raid material).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85829/nightfire-robe">
<img alt="Nightfire Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_leather_raiddruid_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nightfire Robe</span></a> (Leatherworking - requires a phase 1 Raid material).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> (Requires Alchemy). A great pre-raid trinket that you can craft before you even hit max level.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77535/camouflage-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Camouflage Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Camouflage Retinal Armor</span></a> (Requires Engineering). A good pre-raid helm though replaced more quickly in phase 2.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Restoration Druids</span></h2>Our <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84736/natures-focus">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_90.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nature's Focus</span></a> passive gives us a 100% hit chance, which means you don't need to worry about getting Hit or Expertise and can focus on other stats.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Restoration Druids</span></h2>Our gem choices are fairly straightforward and we'll hit our socket bonuses too, since we have good gems in every color. Avoid pure secondary gems. They are worse at this gear level than hybrid Intellect gems but may come into focus later in the expansion.<br/>
<br/>In Phase 1 we gemmed to maximize socket bonuses and intellect. As the expansion goes on, pure secondary gems will rise in value relative to intellect gems. In Phase 3, freshly geared characters can continue the intellect-focused gem strategy but geared characters (520+ ilvl) can start considering pure secondary gems. <b>The difference between these two gem sets is small.</b>
<br/>
<br/>
